Fix #1:
    Error: link.c, line 26, found using gdb command "where" after a segmentation fault
    Problem: The func createList() failed to allocate memory before trying to copy the input string to node->data
    Solution: create->data = malloc(firstE) to allocate the space for the string before copying input string over

Fix #2:
    Error: link.c, line 54, found using "where" and "list" to better view the context of the line
    Problem: prev and cur nodes were initiated, but cur was never pointed to the list pointer so it didn't have a node to read
    Solution: cur = *list, makes our cur node the head node of the given list so we can start the loop comparison strcmp condition

Fix #3:
    Error: link.c, line 76, found using where and print to examine variables to see if the loop crashed on iteration 1 or further in
    Problem: link was never set to any node, so when dest = link, dest was not set to any meaningful node in the llist
    Solution: before the while loop, set link to dest->next so its a valid node in the llist, or NULL if only 1 node exists